    <dataSetInformation>
      <common:UUID>769eb49f-4841-495a-a4f7-bc6ebe94fac2</common:UUID>
      <name>
        <baseName xml:lang="en">Clinker_at production, IT </baseName>
      </name>
      <common:synonyms>Clinker, alla produzione, IT</common:synonyms>
      <classificationInformation>
        <common:classification name="ILCDCategories" classes="../ILCDClassification.xml">
          <common:class level="0">Systems</common:class>
          <common:class level="1">Construction</common:class>
        </common:classification>
      </classificationInformation>
      <common:generalComment>Dataset developed according to Arcadia project Methodology (Report: “Metodologia per gli studi di filiera della Banca Dati italiana LCA”). LCA study of Cement production (report: “STUDIO LCA DELLA FILIERA DEL CEMENTO”). The dataset refers to the production of clinker in Italy that is in input to the main types of cement defined by the UNI EN 197-1. Data have been provided by AITEC/Federbeton and collected for the development of the EPD (Environmental Product Declaration) of the Italian medium gray cement.</common:generalComment>
      <referenceToExternalDocumentation type="source data set" refObjectId="dc6b35dd-18a1-4437-86d1-756c9972c914" version="01.00.000" uri="../sources/dc6b35dd-18a1-4437-86d1-756c9972c914.xml">
        <common:shortDescription>Sposato P., Luciano A., Corrado S., Altamura P., Rinaldi C., 2023. “STUDIO LCA DELLA FILIERA DEL CEMENTO”. Internal report ARCADIA Project. &#13;
Background datasets from Ecoinvent database cut-off (v.3.7.1) were used for the LCA study&#13;
</common:shortDescription>
      </referenceToExternalDocumentation>
    </dataSetInformation>
    <quantitativeReference type="Reference flow(s)">
      <referenceToReferenceFlow>0</referenceToReferenceFlow>
    </quantitativeReference>
    <time>
      <common:referenceYear>2020</common:referenceYear>
      <common:dataSetValidUntil>2025</common:dataSetValidUntil>
    </time>
    <geography>
      <locationOfOperationSupplyOrProduction location="IT">
        <descriptionOfRestrictions>Data collected from Italian average clinker production</descriptionOfRestrictions>
      </locationOfOperationSupplyOrProduction>
    </geography>
    <technology>
      <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>1t of clinker produced in Italy.&#13;
Clinker is produced from natural raw materials (such as limestone, clay, gypsum, marl and others) which are crushed, finely ground, homogenised and fired in a blast furnace. Once out, the clinker is cooled.  All the processes of the clinker production stages, including transports and emissions to air, are foreground processes, modelled using primary data.&#13;
Particularly:&#13;
•	Average data provided by the Italian Cement Techno-Economic Association (AITEC) for the years 2019 and 2020, representing 16.4% and 17% of national production respectively.Data provided by AITEC/Federbeton have been collected for the development of the EPD (Environmental Product Declaration) of the italian medium gray cement.&#13;
•	National average emission factors for the year 2019 (ISPRA, 2019) relating to clinker production (blast furnace process).&#13;
•	The study by Rigamonti et al. (2012) for modeling secondary solid fuel (SSF) production&#13;
•	Water consumption is modelled using primary data provided by a company part of the working group&#13;
&#13;
 For the background processes (raw material in input) EcoInvent database (v. 3.7.1) cut-off datasets were used. &#13;
</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
      <technologicalApplicability>Production of italian average clinker for construction sector</technologicalApplicability>
    </technology>
  </processInformation>
